From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: ov5640: autofocus and control fixes from megi's tree

The OV5640 drives its lens motor (VCM) from an internal microcontroller
that runs OmniVision's autofocus firmware; mainline never loads it, so the
lens stays at rest. This is drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c from Ondrej Jirman's
(megi) cams-7.2 branch (https://codeberg.org/megi/linux, de799fc8136e):

- loads ov5640_af.bin into the sensor at power-on and hands it commands:
  V4L2_CID_FOCUS_AUTO (continuous), AUTO_FOCUS_START/STOP/STATUS,
  FOCUS_ABSOLUTE (0-1023) and a focus zone control;
- fixes to the exposure, gain, white balance, contrast, saturation and hue
  controls, a brightness control, denoising and sharpening off, AE target
  lowered (52 -> 28);
- the chip ID is checked at power-on instead of at probe, system
  suspend/resume through runtime PM.

The autofocus commits build on the others, so the whole file is taken.

---
